                  "resource_id": "levelled_description",
                  "stats": {
                    "id": "levelled_description_b190dcd64cd1",
                    "level": {
                      "value": 1
                    },
                    "description": {
                      "value": "You can exert your unsettling presence to subtly Demoralize others. When you do, Demoralize loses the auditory trait and gains the visual trait, and you don't take a penalty when you attempt to Demoralize a creature that doesn't understand your language. You also gain the Invigorating Fear reaction. Your alternate form is a fox, which has the statistics of 1st-level pest form.\n\n**Invigorating Fear**\n\n- **Activate:** Reaction\n- **Frequency:** once per hour\n- **Trigger:** A creature within 60 feet gains the frightened condition.\n\nYou are invigorated by the shock of a prank or the thrum of terror. You gain temporary Hit Points equal to the creature's level or 3, whichever is higher. You lose any temporary Hit Points after 1 minute."
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
